<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!--
================================================================================
FinForge Excel Add-in - Custom Ribbon UI Definition
================================================================================

DESCRIPTION:
Office Open XML (ECMA-376) ribbon definition for the FinForge Excel add-in.
Defines the custom "FinForge" ribbon tab with a "Dashboard" button that
launches the portfolio management GUI.

FORMAT:
This file uses Microsoft's Fluent Ribbon Extensibility Framework (RibbonX).
It is an XML-based ribbon customization format used by Excel 2007 and later.

STRUCTURE:
- customUI: Root element (version="1.0" for Excel 2007-2016, "1.1"+ for later)
- ribbon: Ribbon UI container
  - tabs: Collection of ribbon tabs
    - tab: Single ribbon tab ("FinForge")
      - group: Logical group of controls
        - button: Clickable button control ("Dashboard")

ATTRIBUTES:
- id: Unique identifier (used in VBA callbacks)
- label: Display text shown to user
- image: Icon image (optional, uses default if omitted)
- onAction: VBA macro called when control is activated
- size: Control size ("large", "normal")

EVENT CALLBACKS:
- onAction="LaunchDashboard": Maps to LaunchDashboard() subroutine in VBA
- onLoad="OnRibbonLoad": Maps to OnRibbonLoad() subroutine in VBA

ICON IMAGES:
- Currently uses built-in Excel image (no custom icon)
- To add custom icon: Replace image="" with image="idemoticon"
- Icons must be base64-encoded PNG or embedded as Office Art XML

NOTE ON NAMESPACE:
- Namespace: http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/2006/01/customui
- This is the standard namespace for Excel 2007+ ribbon customization
- Do NOT change the namespace URL

ASSEMBLY INSTRUCTIONS:
This XML must be embedded in the XLAM file at the path:
  customUI/customUI1.xml

This requires manual editing of the XLAM's internal ZIP structure.
See: FinForge_addin/AddIn_Assembly_Instructions.md for detailed steps.

TESTING:
After assembly:
1. Open Excel
2. File > Options > Trust Center > Trust Center Settings > Trusted Locations
3. Add the XLAM file's directory as trusted
4. Enable the add-in (File > Options > Add-ins > Manage Excel Add-ins)
5. Close and reopen Excel
6. Look for "FinForge" tab in the ribbon
7. Click "Dashboard" button to test

TROUBLESHOOTING:
- Ribbon not showing: Check CustomUI1.xml path in XLAM package (use WinRAR/7-Zip)
- Button not working: Verify VBA is not in edit mode; check Excel Macro Security
- Error messages: Enable "Developer" tab for error details in VBA IDE
- XML syntax error: Validate XML with online validator if ribbon doesn't appear

================================================================================
-->

<customUI xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/2006/01/customui" onLoad="OnRibbonLoad">
  
  <ribbon startFromScratch="false">
    
    <tabs>
      
      <!-- FinForge Tab: Main ribbon tab for the add-in -->
      <tab id="finforgeTab" label="FinForge">
        
        <!-- Main Group: Contains primary controls for FinForge -->
        <group id="mainGroup" label="Dashboard">
          
          <!-- Dashboard Button: Launch portfolio management application -->
          <button
              id="dashboardButton"
              label="Dashboard"
              imageMso="PowerPointSlideShowFromCurrent"
              size="large"
              onAction="LaunchDashboard"
              screentip="Launch FinForge Dashboard"
              supertip="Click to open the FinForge portfolio dashboard. This will launch the main application in a new window."
          />
          
        </group>
        
        <!-- Info Group: Help and documentation (placeholder for future) -->
        <group id="infoGroup" label="Help">
          
          <!-- Placeholder for future help/documentation button -->
          <!-- Uncomment below to add Help button in future versions:
          
          <button
              id="helpButton"
              label="Help"
              imageMso="Help"
              size="normal"
              onAction="ShowHelp"
              screentip="FinForge Help"
              supertip="Open FinForge documentation and user guide."
          />
          
          -->
          
        </group>
        
      </tab>
      
    </tabs>
    
  </ribbon>
  
</customUI>

<!--
================================================================================
RIBBON XML ATTRIBUTE REFERENCE
================================================================================

BUTTON ATTRIBUTES:
- id: Unique identifier within the ribbon (used in VBA callbacks)
- label: Text displayed on the button
- imageMso: Built-in Excel icon ID (e.g., "PowerPointSlideShowFromCurrent")
  Available icons: https://officeribbonxeditor.codeplex.com/
- image: Custom image ID (requires manual image embedding)
- size: "large" (normal icon) or "normal" (smaller icon)
- onAction: VBA macro name to call when button is clicked
- screentip: Tooltip text shown on hover
- supertip: Extended tooltip (multi-line help text)
- enabled: true/false to enable/disable button at startup

COMMON ICON IDs (imageMso):
- PowerPointSlideShowFromCurrent: Play icon
- Help: Question mark icon
- Refresh: Refresh icon
- Save: Save icon
- Open: Open file icon
- Print: Print icon
- Settings: Gear icon
- Calculator: Calculator icon
- ChartInsertColumn: Chart icon

GROUP ATTRIBUTES:
- id: Unique identifier for group
- label: Group label text (shown if label is set)

TAB ATTRIBUTES:
- id: Unique identifier for tab
- label: Tab name shown in ribbon

RIBBON ATTRIBUTES:
- startFromScratch: false = add to existing ribbon; true = replace entire ribbon
- onLoad: VBA macro called when ribbon initializes

================================================================================
EXAMPLE: ADDING A SECOND BUTTON
================================================================================

To add another button to the Dashboard group, add this inside <group id="mainGroup">:

  <button
      id="refreshButton"
      label="Refresh Data"
      imageMso="Refresh"
      size="large"
      onAction="RefreshData"
      screentip="Refresh Stock Data"
      supertip="Update all stock data from Yahoo Finance."
  />

Then create the corresponding VBA subroutine in RibbonCallback.vba:

  Sub RefreshData(control As IRibbonControl)
      ' Your refresh logic here
  End Sub

================================================================================
-->